<title>BRAZIL: Brazil coffee to cool but no frost seen - Somar.</title>
<headline>Brazil coffee to cool but no frost seen - Somar.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>An approaching cold air mass poses no frost threat to Brazil's coffee regions where minimum temperatures are not expected to fall below five degrees Celsius, independent local meteorologists Somar said.</p>
<p>The air mass will cause widespread frosts in the south of the country from the early morning of May 23.</p>
<p>&quot;But there is no forecast of frosts in the coffee regions where there will only colder weather, that is temperatures of around five degrees Celsius,&quot; Somar said.</p>
<p>Minimum temperatures in traditionally cooler coffee regions are currently around 11 degrees Celsius.</p>
<p>Brazil's coffee regions face the greatest frost risk in the months of June and July. ((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
